            <ArticleTitle>Right coronary ostial plasty without patch material.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>396-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Isolated right coronary ostial stenosis may require coronary revascularisation during an open-heart operation, especially during aortic valve replacement. We describe here a new method of right coronary ostial plasty without patch material.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
